From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zink: pair a display-only DRM device with a render-only Vulkan GPU

On Tegra with NVIDIA's nvgpu driver, the GPU is not a DRM device: its Vulkan
device reports no DRM node (VK_EXT_physical_device_drm hasPrimary/hasRender
false), while the only DRM device is the display controller (tegra-drm).
zink_get_display_device() then finds no Vulkan device for the DRM fd it is
given (GBM, EGL), and Zink fails with "failed to choose pdev".

When no Vulkan device matches the DRM device and exactly one Vulkan device
has no DRM node at all, pair them. The screen keeps the display fd, which it
needs to turn dma-bufs into KMS handles, as kmsro does for other
render-only/display-only pairs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -1713,11 +1713,30 @@
       .pNext = &drm_props,
    };
 
+   int no_node = -1, no_node_count = 0;
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < pdev_count; ++i) {
+      drm_props.hasPrimary = drm_props.hasRender = VK_FALSE;
       VKSCR(GetPhysicalDeviceProperties2)(pdevs[i], &props);
       if (drm_props.renderMajor == dev_major &&
           drm_props.renderMinor == dev_minor)
          return i;
+      if (!drm_props.hasPrimary && !drm_props.hasRender) {
+         no_node = i;
+         no_node_count++;
+      }
+   }
+
+   /* Render-only GPU next to a separate display controller (for example the NVIDIA nvgpu
+    * driver on Tegra, which is not a DRM device, beside tegra-drm): the DRM device we were
+    * given belongs to no Vulkan device. If exactly one Vulkan device has no DRM node at all,
+    * it is the GPU behind this display: pair them, and keep the display fd for KMS handles.
+    */
+   if (no_node_count == 1) {
+      VKSCR(GetPhysicalDeviceProperties2)(pdevs[no_node], &props);
+      mesa_logw("ZINK: no Vulkan device for DRM device %d:%d; pairing it with %s, "
+                "the only device without a DRM node", (int)dev_major, (int)dev_minor,
+                props.properties.deviceName);
+      return no_node;
    }
 
    return -1;
